{
    "attributes": {
        "author": [
            "Partner Threat Feed"
        ],
        "description": "Identifies processes started from binaries whose SHA-256 hash matches a Nickel Valise botnet sample, as reported in campaign PTF-02298. The indicators are synthetic and use reserved address and domain ranges, so they match no real traffic.",
        "false_positives": [
            "Security testing that replays known indicators.",
            "A shared hosting address or domain that later served benign content."
        ],
        "from": "now-9m",
        "index": [
            "logs-endpoint.events.process-*"
        ],
        "language": "eql",
        "license": "Elastic License v2",
        "name": "Nickel Valise Botnet: Process started from known malicious binary (PTF-02298)",
        "note": "## Triage and analysis\n\n### Investigating Nickel Valise Botnet: Process started from known malicious binary\n\nThis rule matches indicators that the Partner Threat Feed attributes to the Nickel Valise botnet in campaign PTF-02298.\n\n### Possible investigation steps\n\n- Review the matching event and the host or user it came from.\n- Look for other indicators from the same campaign on the same host.\n- Check the process tree around the event for the initial execution or delivery.\n\n### Response and remediation\n\n- Isolate the host if the match is confirmed.\n- Block the indicators at the network edge and on endpoints.\n- Reset credentials used on the host.\n",
        "query": "process where event.type == \"start\" and process.hash.sha256 in (\"20bfec57eac71ad3587590e70fa662a635cebf80d0f95bf07fac38b1bdb6256f\", \"de10f52d3dca526ba7ede734f7e6dbb56a460ff1ce5e46c42f897a465c9e2b64\", \"07fdf2506a0cb1ef940e17617b55798e86e9585f026578385d6ab41806970564\", \"1b9cdb09b558f885ed9975008e2596ccb498c04428589aafff211cd5038bb416\", \"116f3f3a3b68af18d86ea902439f85ae44c1c2885884935456dc71f81e0d801d\", \"67159366b49f8a66a66ef879787b2686a2f841c2497576dec7669524bb87ffa9\", \"2b47047349d40f77950e1b0f4d6801f482b211442d1b80502af4efcec05f4433\", \"65749138060c1099f18001804dde2867f7fd18063fc48d349a37cd6110bac99b\")",
        "references": [
